Package: @alchemy.run/domain
Applies-to: vendor/alchemy/alchemy.run-domain-e1c3e6d.tgz
Upstream: not yet reported
Why: When a decision's `keyOf` builds an instance's id from two fields (`${cmd.importId}/${cmd.row}`), the prover
  replays the solver's answer under an empty id, on a stream the real `keyOf` never reads. A rule the decision
  breaks then comes back "not proved", with no state to look at. With this it comes back "violated", with the state,
  the command and the events.
Remove-when: The library reads a computed id back with the inputs. `bun run beep patches prove` then says this
  patch's test passes without it.
Test: test/alchemy-domain/01-computed-instance-id/ComputedInstanceId.test.ts

